 4348 073413             ! ============================================================
 4349 073413             ! PLOTP RUNTIME -- implementation inherited from v0.10a
 4350 073413             !
 4351 073413             !       PLOTP x,y,f
 4352 073413             !
 4353 073413             ! f=1:
 4354 073413             !       Hybrid operation.
 4355 073413             !       1. ROM360 MOVE x,y ; DRAW x,y ; MOVE x,y
 4356 073413             !          -> CRT/plotter graphics path, ending pen-up at the point.
Page   78                                                             
CAPASM

 4357 073413             !       2. Independently map x,y through the active ROM360 SCALE and
 4358 073413             !          explicitly SET the corresponding CRT pixel if it lies on-screen.
 4359 073413             !          This guarantees the raster result even if a zero-length DRAW is
 4360 073413             !          not rendered as a CRT pixel by the ROM360 vector path.
 4361 073413             !
 4362 073413             ! f=0:
 4363 073413             !       CRT-only CLEAR of the mapped pixel.  No plotter output.
 4364 073413             !
 4365 073413             ! f=2:
 4366 073413             !       CRT-only XOR of the mapped pixel.  No plotter output.
 4367 073413             !
 4368 073413             ! Invalid f values are a no-op, matching LINE semantics.
 4369 073413             !
 4370 073413             ! PLOTP deliberately reuses PAINT's PX/PY/PF, PMODE, PXC/PYC, PTARG and
 4371 073413             ! ROWBUF helpers.  Commands are not re-entrant, so no additional large
 4372 073413             ! working area is required.
 4373 073413             ! ============================================================
 4374 073413             
 4375 073413 241                 BYT 241
 4376 073414             
 4377 073414 232         PLTPRT.   SAD
 4378 073415 230                 BIN
